*******************************************************************************
*                             DCODE IDE v0.6                                  *
*                          --- USAGE MANUAL ---                               *
*******************************************************************************

Welcome, DCode IDE is a modern-style development environment for 32-bit DOS.

This manual provides the basic information you need to start coding.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GETTING STARTED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Run DCODE.EXE from your DOS prompt. You can optionally provide a filename:
    C:\> DCODE.EXE MYFILE.C ANOTHER.C ...

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FILE OPERATIONS:
    Ctrl + N            : Create a New File
    Ctrl + O            : Quick Open File Dialog (interactive directory browser)
    Ctrl + Shift + S    : Save Current File
    Alt + F4            : Close Current File / Window Split
    Esc                 : Exit DCode IDE (prompts to save if modified)

WINDOW SPLITS:
    Ctrl + \            : Split Active Window Vertically (shares the same file tab)
    Ctrl + W            : Cycle Active Cursor Focus between Window Splits

NAVIGATION & SELECTION:
    Arrow Keys          : Move cursor Up, Down, Left, Right
    Home / End          : Jump to Start / End of Line
    Page Up / Page Down : Jump to Top / Bottom of File
    Ctrl + Left/Right   : Jump cursor word-by-word horizontally
    Alt + Up/Down       : Swap/Move current line Up or Down
    Alt + Shift         : Open File Switcher Overlay (hold Alt, press Shift)

EDITING:
    Enter               : Create New Line (with auto-indent)
    Backspace           : Delete character to the left
    Delete              : Delete character at cursor (forward)
    Tab                 : Insert Tab (configurable size and indicator lines)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. VIDEO & DISPLAY MODES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DCode IDE supports cycling through various VGA text modes to adjust screen 
density and column width on DOS.

    F11                 : Cycle Video Modes
    F12                 : Toggle Video Memory Map Viewer (FOR DEBUG)

Supported modes:
    - VID_80X25 (1)     : Standard 80x25 text mode (Default)
    - VID_80X43 (2)     : High-density 80x43 text mode
    - VID_80X50 (3)     : High-density 80x50 text mode
    - VID_132X50 (7)    : Wide 132x50 text mode
    - VID_132X60 (8)    : Wide 132x60 text mode
    *(Modes 4, 5, 6 are reserved / not supported yet)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. INTERACTIVE UTILITIES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

QUICK OPEN DIALOG (Ctrl + O):
    - Opens a centered popup listing files in the current folder.
    - Pre-fills the current absolute path in an editable text prompt.
    - Use Left/Right arrows to move cursor within the path prompt.
    - Use Up/Down arrows to select files/folders from the list.
    - Press Enter to open files or navigate directories (select '..' to go up).
    - Press Esc to close the dialog.

FILE SWITCHER (Alt + Shift):
    - Displays an overlay list of tabs opened in the current window.
    - Hold the 'Alt' key and press 'Shift' to cycle through the tabs.
    - The selected tab is marked with an asterisk (*).
    - Release the 'Alt' key to switch to the selected tab.
    - Runs asynchronously without blocking screen animations or cursor.

WINDOW SPLITTING (Ctrl + \):
    - Divides the active pane into side-by-side splits.
    - Shared editor view: editing in one pane will immediately sync the edits
      into the adjacent split pane.
    - Closing all tabs within a split closes the pane, stretching the neighboring
      pane to fit the reclaimed width automatically.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. STARTUP CONFIGURATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Global settings and colors are customized via "DEFAULT.CFG". 

Key settings include:
    DEBUG               : Set to 1 to enable logs to LOGS.TXT, 0 to disable.
    MAX_FILE_INSTANCE_SIZE : Max file instance size in kilobytes (default 512).
    MAX_FILE_INSTANCES_OPENED : Max concurrent open files (default 32).
    AUTOIDENTING        : Enable auto-indentation on new lines (0/1).
    AUTOCLOSING         : Enable auto-closing parenthesis/quotes (0/1).
    AUTOBRACES          : Enable auto-braces matching (0/1).
    TAB_INDICATOR       : Highlight tab indentation with visual lines (0/1).
    TAB_SPACE_INDICATOR : Highlight spaces indentation (0/1).
    DEFAULT_EXTENSION   : Default extension for new files (e.g. .c).
    DEFAULT_VIDEO_MODE  : Startup video mode index (1-8, defaults to 1).
    STATUSBAR_COLOR_BG  : Background color code (0-15) for status bar.
    STATUSBAR_COLOR_TEXT: Foreground color code (0-15) for status bar.
    DW_RESWORD_*        : Custom C syntax highlighting colors (0-15).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. TIPS & DEBUGGING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Check the bottom right status bar to see if the file is marked "MODIFIED"
  before quitting.
- Status bar messages last for 5 seconds or disappear upon cursor movement.
- If rendering issues occur after switching modes or loading large files,
  use F11 to cycle through display modes to refresh the screen buffer.

